# NestJS Module Dependency Rules

Consult this rule **before adding any `imports: [...]` entry** in a `*.module.ts`.

## Module tiers (imports flow downward only)

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph tier3 [Tier3_Domain]
    Bookings[BookingsModule]
    Payments[PaymentsModule]
    Notifications[NotificationsModule]
    Shops[ShopsModule]
  end
  subgraph tier2 [Tier2_CrossCutting]
    Auth[AuthModule]
    Rating[RatingModule]
    Whatsapp[WhatsappModule]
  end
  subgraph tier1 [Tier1_Utility]
    Messaging[MessagingModule]
  end

  Bookings --> Messaging
  Bookings --> Payments
  Bookings --> Notifications
  Payments --> Messaging
  Notifications --> Messaging
  Notifications --> Bookings
```

| Tier | Modules | May import | Must NOT import |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Utility (leaf)** | `MessagingModule` | `ConfigModule`, `AuthModule`, `BullModule`, own entities only | Any domain module (`Bookings`, `Payments`, `Notifications`, `Shops`) |
| **Domain** | `Bookings`, `Payments`, `Shops`, etc. | Utility modules; peer modules **one-way only** | Must not cause utility modules to import back |
| **Cross-cutting** | `Auth`, `Rating`, `Whatsapp` | Utility + infra | Domain business modules (unless explicitly exported API) |

**Hard rule:** If module A imports B, then B must not import A (directly or transitively). `forwardRef` is a last resort, not the default.

---

## Principle: low-level accepts data, high-level fetches data

Utility modules must not load domain data. Callers query the DB, build inputs, then call the utility.

### MSG91 example (canonical)

**Bad — causes tier inversion or hidden cycles:**

- `MessagingModule` imports `BookingsModule` or runs booking SQL internally
- `MessagingDispatchService` accepts `bookingId` and loads customer phone itself

**Good — current implementation:**

- [`MessagingDispatchPort`](src/modules/messaging/ports/messaging-dispatch.port.ts) accepts fully hydrated `SendBookingMessageInput` (`shopId`, `bookingId`, `recipient`, `variables`)
- Callers own DB lookup:
  - [`PaymentStateMachineService`](src/modules/payments/payment-state-machine.service.ts) → `BOOKING_PAYMENT.findMessagingContext()`
  - [`BookingsService`](src/modules/bookings/bookings.service.ts) → `BOOKING_REPOSITORY.findMessagingContext()`
  - [`BookingReminderProcessor`](src/modules/notifications/booking-reminder.processor.ts) → `BOOKING_REPOSITORY` (exported from BookingsModule)

Inject via port tokens (`MESSAGING_DISPATCH`, `BOOKING_REPOSITORY`) — not concrete adapter classes.

