## Pre-import checklist

Run before merging any `*.module.ts` change:

- [ ] Draw the import arrow: does the target module already import me (directly or via a third module)?
- [ ] Can the dependency be inverted via a **port + adapter** in the importing module instead?
- [ ] Can the callee accept **pre-hydrated input** instead of importing the caller's module?
- [ ] If exporting a repository token, export the **token only** — not adapters or internal services
- [ ] If `forwardRef` is required, add a one-line comment explaining the cycle
- [ ] Run `pnpm run build` — Nest DI fails loudly on unresolved circular deps at bootstrap

---

## Forbidden patterns (flag in review)

| Pattern | Why bad | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Utility module imports domain module | Inverts tier hierarchy | Caller hydrates inputs |
| Service imports another module's TypeORM entity/adapter | Bypasses ports | Inject port token |
| Both modules import each other without `forwardRef` | Nest bootstrap failure | Refactor or `forwardRef` + comment |
| `forwardRef` to avoid extracting shared port | Masks design smell | Extract lookup/persistence module |
| Exporting adapters from feature modules | Leaks infra, tightens coupling | Export service or port token only |

